## Context

The frontier deep-research benchmark (`query_frontier`) ran 14 models × 3 prompts
(inventory, scenarios, skill) ad hoc.  Results live in `experiments/outputs/frontier/`,
`frontier_scenarios/`, and `frontier_skill/` with a hand-written SUMMARY.md.

Two gaps:

1. **No Make target.** `query_frontier` is the only query module with no Makefile
   integration — it was invoked manually.
2. **No measurements.** Results are not fed into `measurements.jsonl`, so they
   are invisible to the reporting pipeline (tables, self-consistency, etc.).

## Desired behavior

- The frontier deep-research condition is declared in `experiments.toml` alongside
  the other conditions (census, rag, multiturn, web, decomposed, sourced).
- Config specifies: prompt(s), model set, repeat count, budget, max_tokens,
  temperature, and output directory — same fields the other conditions use, plus
  the frontier-specific parameters (high max_tokens, temperature 0).
- `make frontier` (or the condition name chosen under ticket 0024) runs the
  benchmark reproducibly.
- Results are extracted into `measurements.jsonl` by `sweep-summary` or
  equivalent, so they appear in report tables.
- Existing cached outputs in `outputs/frontier*` are recognized and skipped
  (the skip-if-cached logic in `query_frontier` already works; the pipeline
  just needs to invoke it).

## What this ticket is NOT

- Not about changing `query_frontier.py` internals.
- Not about the Worker migration (ticket 0011).
- Not about renaming sweeps (ticket 0024) — use whatever naming that ticket lands on.

## Test

`make frontier` succeeds with cached outputs (no API calls), and at least one
frontier result row appears in `measurements.jsonl`.

## Exit criteria

- Frontier condition declared in `experiments.toml`
- Make target exists and is documented in `make help`
- Frontier results flow into `measurements.jsonl`
